  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Minnesota recorded $1.5B in federal contract obligations for FY2026 to date. The state had 25,791 awards with an average award size of $58.7K, and obligations fell 39.2% year over year. Obligations have varied across the last six fiscal years: FY21 $2.6B, FY22 $2.4B, FY23 $2.7B, FY24 $3B, FY25 $2.5B, and FY26 $1.5B. The Department of Defense is the largest buyer so far in FY2026, followed by the Department of Veterans Affairs and the Department of Agriculture. NORTHROP GRUMMAN SYSTEMS CORPORATION leads vendors by obligations, followed by MCGOUGH CONSTRUCTION CO., LLC and BAE SYSTEMS LAND & ARMAMENTS L.P. Ammunition (except Small Arms) Manufacturing is the largest industry by obligations, followed by Commercial and Institutional Building Construction and Cheese Manufacturing. All figures are contract obligations and current-year totals are partial (fiscal year to date).",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "What changed in Minnesota federal contracting year over year?",
        "body": "Obligations fell 39.2% year over year. FY26 obligations are $1.5B compared with prior fiscal years that ranged from $2.4B to $3B. The average award size in FY2026 to date is $58.7K across 25,791 awards. These figures reflect contract obligations through FY2026 to date, a partial fiscal-year total."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Who are the biggest buyers and industries in Minnesota this fiscal year?",
        "body": "The Department of Defense obligated $468M, the Department of Veterans Affairs obligated $255M, and the Department of Agriculture obligated $253M in FY2026 to date. Ammunition (except Small Arms) Manufacturing accounts for $185M in obligations, Commercial and Institutional Building Construction accounts for $126M, and Cheese Manufacturing accounts for $95M. Those agencies and industries drive the largest shares of obligations in the state for FY2026 to date."
      }
    ]
  },
